  "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=2.5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{2.5}{2}=1.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=2.5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|1.25|=1.25$ centered at the point $(1.25,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/110736084be735e5e103fe6c541cc3f98140743495cc7d23cbb2242c0eade076.png)",
